{
  "version": 2,
  "notes": [
    "The concept key is the identity; the label is an attribute. Renaming a label is an",
    "edit, renaming a key is a data migration.",
    "",
    "broader is a DAG, not a tree: a concept may sit under several parents, and the",
    "existing data needs it - Python is a language and is used in data and in ML, and",
    "forcing one parent was what made the old flat category field lossy.",
    "",
    "Two parent axes. type.* says what kind of thing a concept is; area.* says where it",
    "is used. Every skill carries exactly one type and zero or more areas.",
    "",
    "Labels are matched case-insensitively with word-like boundaries that treat # + . as",
    "part of a token, so C# cannot match inside C#-adjacent and C cannot match inside C++.",
    "",
    "ambiguous lists surface forms that indicate a concept but cannot be trusted to mean",
    "it - Go, R, C and Julia are ordinary words or names. A hit on one is recorded as an",
    "unresolved mention and never asserted, so the size of the gap stays measurable",
    "instead of being silently dropped.",
    "",
    "requiresCapital marks concepts whose label is also an ordinary English word but which",
    "are normally capitalised. They match only where the text kept a capital, so REST API",
    "counts and the rest of the team does not."
  ],
